# Byte pins for the manual packs /opt/strata/bin/fetch_models.sh stages
# (cf-86 C01 SC117 pair + C02 orcarouter pair), sourced by that driver.
#
# Why a sourced file instead of literals on the download legs: the legs, the
# pack contract and the test suite all need the same numbers, and the
# values.yaml heredocs kept them next to the code that used them only as long
# as the code lived in the chart. Two homes for one literal is how a shard
# pin drifts; this file is the single home (C07 lift, U9.4).
#
# Provenance: HF tree API read anonymously 2026-10-30 — lfs.size per shard, the
# exact values the staged packs were built and delivered against. hf_fetch.py
# renames a .part only on an EXACT size match, so a literal that drifts by even
# a few hundred bytes is a silently truncated shard entering iq_pack. Re-read
# the tree before touching one.

# SC117/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-abliterated-GGUF, IQ3_XXS tier, 2 shards.
# Shard 2 is the 28.8 GB n-gram (PLE) table.
ABL_IQ3_XXS_SHARD1=47342144896
ABL_IQ3_XXS_SHARD2=28800138432

# orcarouter/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Uncensored-GGUF, IQ3_XXS tier, 2 shards —
# gated bytes, public metadata. Σ 85202668032 = ORCA.md's 85.20 GB.
ORCA_IQ3_XXS_SHARD1=44637691008
ORCA_IQ3_XXS_SHARD2=40564977024
